---
import ToolLayoutEn from '../../layouts/ToolLayoutEn.astro';
import FormatConvert from '../../components/tools/en/FormatConvert.tsx';
---
<ToolLayoutEn slug="format-convert">
  <FormatConvert client:load />
  <div slot="seo-content">
    <h2>Online Image Format Converter</h2>
    <p>Convert between JPG, PNG, WebP, and AVIF with adjustable quality and batch processing. AVIF is the most advanced image format in 2026, delivering 20-30% smaller files than WebP at the same quality. All conversion is done locally in your browser using native Canvas and createImageBitmap APIs—no uploads, no servers.</p>
    <h3>Format Comparison</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>JPG</strong>: Lossy, no transparency support, widest compatibility, ideal for photographs.</li>
      <li><strong>PNG</strong>: Lossless, supports transparency, larger file size, ideal for icons and line art.</li>
      <li><strong>WebP</strong>: Lossy or lossless, supports transparency and animation, small file size, modern standard.</li>
      <li><strong>AVIF</strong>: Lossy or lossless, supports transparency and animation, smallest file size, the most advanced format in 2026.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>About AVIF</h3>
    <p>AVIF is based on AV1 video coding. As of 2026 it is fully supported by Chrome 85+, Safari 16+, and Firefox 86+, covering over 95% of the market. It offers the highest compression ratio of any image format today, though encoding is 3-5x slower than WebP, making it best suited for offline conversion of static assets. This tool lets you convert existing images to AVIF with a single click.</p>
  </div>
</ToolLayoutEn>
